 Develop a clear understanding of Ciena’s integrated photonic components to develop innovative new opto-mechanical design s ;   
 Work with both the RF design and optical chip design teams to define   functional   specifications and interface efficiently all design components;   
 Plan design of experiment to   ensure   that all critical design parameters are met, while optimizing cost and assembly for high volume manufacturing;   
 Monitor, document and communicate advancements and raise potential issues that may have influence on product functionality or target dates;   
 Ensure the appropriate documentation is created;   
 Participate and organize design reviews, ensure documentation and follow-up;   
 Interact with other external groups ( production ramp-up   and operation groups) to transfer the developed design into a production environment.   
 The Must Haves:    
 A bachelor’s degree in   mechanical   engineering or related discipline with a minimum of   3   years of   design   experience in a technology - oriented and product development environment.    
 Team player with the ability to develop strong relationships in a multi-disciplinary environment;   
 Ability to effectively organize work in a multi-tasks and fast-paced environment strongly driven by product development schedule;   
 Be rigorous, be well organized and structured, have sense of initiative and a strong desire for innovation and problem solving;   
 Ability to clearly communicate (synthesis) in a proactive and solutions-focused manner;   
 Nice to Haves: 
 Proficiency in the Creo design software;   
 Experience and/or knowledge   of the   design of photonic components, thermo-mechanical stresses optimization, IC assembly processes   or   optical design;   
 Experience and/or knowledge in Finite Element Analysis (ANSYS) ;   
 Deep knowledge of electronics and optics packaging, for example lasers or modulators;   
 Fiber coupling to optical waveguides;   
